The numbers is a list of 2, 6, 4, 8, 10, 9, and 15.
The ordered is an empty list of whole numbers.
For each value in numbers.
Place value into ordered.

Sort ordered.
The first is -1.
The farthest is -1.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of numbers.
If item spot of numbers is not item spot of ordered.
If first is less than 0, set first to spot.
Set farthest to spot.

If first is less than 0, show 0, otherwise show farthest minus first plus 1.
